#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cc-bundle — queued rows whose briefs name the same file run as ONE worker, chosen and started by the box.

  cc-bundle show <repo> [--json] [--no-net]   the bundles it would run — rows, files, model, name, the rows waiting
                                              behind each — and what holds them right now; nothing to run prints nothing
  cc-bundle go <repo> [--dry-run] [--no-net]  start the first bundle nothing holds, one per call; --dry-run says
                                              which and starts nothing
  cc-bundle --tick                            `go` for every repo with a board — rides cc-reconcile.service
  cc-bundle selfcheck

WHY (owner, 2026-09-12: "How much of the backlog can be consolidated into a few PRs and workers or sub agents?
That should be an automatic process."). Forty-odd rows sat queued, most of them one-file raised- findings, and
each was dispatched one at a time by a seat reading the board — every row buying its own landing (gates, a paid
review read, a merge), and two of them in one file buying a rebase besides. `cc-brief ready` already computes
which queued rows share a file and says "one builder for …"; this is the half that acts on it.

A BUNDLE IS A GROUP `cc-brief ready` PRINTS: two or more queued rows nothing in flight is holding, joined by a
file their briefs name (transitively — a and b sharing one file and b and c another is one bundle). It becomes
ONE board row, `bundle-<file>-<hash>`, carrying ONE brief: a goal for the whole, then each member's brief under
its own heading, verbatim, and the `Closes a, b and c` line that makes the bundle's PR close every member when it
lands (cc-land reads that line off the PR body). Each member stays `queued` and gets `bundle: <row>` on the
board — `queued` because cc-land's closer skips a running row, the field because cc-brief, cc-pulse and cc-digest
read it as "being written" while the bundle row is live, so nothing offers the member twice. A bundle that lands
closes its members; one that is abandoned or removed hands them back to the pool by the same test.

A BUNDLE IS ONE WORKER'S DIFF AND ONE REVIEWER'S READ: at most ROWS_MAX (6) rows, naming at most FILES_MAX (6)
files between them (CC_BUNDLE_ROWS, CC_BUNDLE_FILES). The join is transitive, and the first live tick after #471
offered ONE bundle of 33 rows over 19 files — every queued raised- row, glued through the test suite and two
tools — which no worker finishes and no reviewer reads. A group over a cap is SPLIT ON THE FILE ITS ROWS MOST
SHARE: the rows naming it fill one bundle, narrowest first, up to the caps; a leftover row naming a file that
bundle names waits for it to land (`show` says so: "N wait behind it") and the rest are grouped again the same
way. Bundles offered together never name a file in common, and neither does a bundle offered later while one
is live: a row naming a file a live bundle's members name is no member until that bundle row is done.

WHAT STAYS OUT. A project row stays whole: a brief that says "milestones" or numbers them (M1, M2 — anywhere in
its text), and a row carrying an `agent` mark, warm or cold — `ready` offers a row whose mark went cold, which
is right for a seat that can ask the session, but a bundle asks nobody, and the row is that session's until it
hands it back (`agent ""`). A row in flight or under review is never re-bundled: a member is a row whose status
is `queued` and that has no PR — `ready` also offers a `blocked` row (a landing that died leaves one, with a PR
and commits of its own), and bundling that would redo its work off main, open a second PR for it and close it on
the bundle's Closes line with its own PR still open. A row sharing a file with nothing is not a bundle and is
left to the seat, exactly as today.

WHAT HOLDS A DISPATCH, in order, and `show` names the first that applies:
  · the project is parked — `cc-pause is <repo>`, the check every timer-driven spender makes before it spends
    (DESIGN: a parked board is left untouched, and the judge's read is spend)
  · the landing queue — QUEUE_HOLD (4) or more jobs in ~/.cc/state/land/, any repo: a landing is the slowest
    thing in the flow, and a worker started now would only join the back of it
  · the spend tier — `cc-tier allows goals`: work the box takes on by itself is moderate's and autonomous's
  · a box-wide usage limit — `cc-limit status`: nothing starts until it lifts, as cc-pulse already holds
  · width — CC_BUNDLE_WIDTH (2) bundle rows already live (queued, running or waiting) on the repo's board
  · a bundle refused inside REFUSED_H (24 h) — the judge said no, `cc` said no — is not offered again until the
    set of rows in it changes; the reason is in the log, and the seat reads it there
One bundle per call, so one tick starts at most one worker and the queue hold decides the next.

THE JUDGE STILL READS THE BUNDLED BRIEF: the row goes in through `cc-board add`, the door every brief enters by,
and a refusal there is recorded and the bundle is not started — no CC_BRIEF_MACHINE and no force. The model is
the box's bands (WORKING.md, model policy): Sonnet when the members name ONE file between them and it is outside
the repo's control layer (tests/control-layer, what buys a paid review), Opus otherwise.

EVERYTHING IT DID IS IN ~/.cc/state/bundle/<repo>.jsonl — one line per dispatch, refusal or hold — and a tick that
started nothing prints nothing. Env: CC_BUNDLE_WIDTH · CC_BUNDLE_ROWS · CC_BUNDLE_FILES · CC_BUNDLE_BIN (tests:
where the siblings are) · CC_BOARDS, CC_STATE (cc-brief's, so a test run keeps out of the box's own state).
"""
import collections, fnmatch, glob, hashlib, json, os, re, subprocess, sys, time

BIN = os.environ.get("CC_BUNDLE_BIN") or os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))
QUEUE_HOLD = 4          # landing jobs on disk before no new work is started (owner's line, 2026-09-12)
REFUSED_H = 24          # hours a refused bundle stays off the offer
LOOP = "3"              # iterations a bundle worker gets: one per member is too many, one is too few
ROWS_MAX = 6            # CC_BUNDLE_ROWS: members a bundle carries at most — what one worker finishes in LOOP runs
FILES_MAX = 6           # CC_BUNDLE_FILES: files its members name between them at most — what one reviewer reads
MODELS = {"sonnet": "claude-sonnet-5", "opus": "claude-opus-5"}
# A PROJECT BRIEF, which stays whole: it says "milestones", or it numbers them — M1, M2 — anywhere in its text,
# not only at a line's start: the improve orch's row writes "SHAPE PROPOSED (the orch decides the method): M1 THE
# SCORER …" mid-line, and the line-anchored test let it into a 33-row bundle (2026-09-13).
MILESTONE = re.compile(r"(?i:\bmilestones?\b)|\bM[1-9]\d?\b")


def home():
    return os.path.expanduser("~")


def brief_mod():
    """cc-brief, imported beside THIS copy — it owns `ready` (which rows could start, grouped by the file they
    share), `named` (the files a brief names) and the board reader; nothing here recomputes any of it."""
    if not hasattr(brief_mod, "mod"):
        import importlib.machinery, importlib.util
        s = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("ccbrief", importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader(
            "ccbrief", os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), "cc-brief")))
        brief_mod.mod = importlib.util.module_from_spec(s); s.loader.exec_module(brief_mod.mod)
    return brief_mod.mod


def sh(*cmd, timeout=120, env=None):
    """Run a sibling and hand back the result, or None: a timer job never dies of a command that hung."""
    try:
        return subprocess.run(cmd, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout, env=env)
    except Exception:
        return None


def said(p):
    """The HEAD of what a sibling said, not its tail: a judge refusal ends on "cut those and dispatch again", and a
    record carrying only that does not say what refused or why (the same lesson cc-land's fix dispatch learned)."""
    out = ((p.stderr or "") + (p.stdout or "")).strip() if p is not None else ""
    lines = [ln.strip() for ln in out.splitlines() if ln.strip()]
    return lines[0] if lines else ("no answer" if p is None else f"exit {p.returncode}")


def log_path(repo):
    return os.path.join(home(), ".cc", "state", "bundle", repo + ".jsonl")


def log(repo, event, name, **kw):
    p = log_path(repo)
    os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(p), exist_ok=True)
    with open(p, "a") as fh:
        fh.write(json.dumps({"ts": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime()), "event": event,
                             "name": name, **kw}) + "\n")


def last_hold(repo):
    """The reason the last logged line held on, or "" when the last line was anything else — so a hold that has
    not changed since the last tick is not written again (72 identical lines a day while a queue stays full)."""
    try:
        with open(log_path(repo)) as fh:
            lines = fh.read().splitlines()
    except OSError:
        return ""
    for ln in reversed(lines):
        try:
            j = json.loads(ln)
        except ValueError:
            continue
        return j.get("why", "") if j.get("event") == "held" else ""
    return ""


def refused_recently(repo):
    """The bundle names refused inside REFUSED_H — read back off the log, so a refusal costs one line and no state
    file of its own. A later `dispatched` line for the same name lifts it (the set was fixed and went)."""
    cold = time.time() - REFUSED_H * 3600
    out = {}
    try:
        with open(log_path(repo)) as fh:
            for ln in fh:
                try:
                    j = json.loads(ln)
                except ValueError:
                    continue
                if brief_mod().epoch(j.get("ts")) < cold:
                    continue
                if j.get("event") == "refused":
                    out[j.get("name")] = j.get("why", "")
                elif j.get("event") == "dispatched":
                    out.pop(j.get("name"), None)
    except OSError:
        pass
    return out


def control_layer(root):
    """The globs of the repo's control layer, as paths under `root`. The file describes the tree it sits in
    (`bin/cc-land`, not `core/bin/cc-land`), so each is prefixed with that tree's own place in the checkout."""
    pats = []
    for tree in ("", "core"):
        p = os.path.join(root, tree, "tests", "control-layer")
        try:
            with open(p) as fh:
                lines = [ln.strip() for ln in fh]
        except OSError:
            continue
        pats += [os.path.join(tree, ln) if tree else ln for ln in lines if ln and not ln.startswith("#")]
    return pats


def model_for(files, root):
    """`sonnet` for a bundle that names one file outside the control layer; `opus` for anything wider or that
    touches a gate, the sandbox, the landing — the bands WORKING.md gives, read off what the rows name."""
    if len(files) != 1:
        return "opus"
    f = next(iter(files))
    return "opus" if any(fnmatch.fnmatch(f, pat) for pat in control_layer(root)) else "sonnet"


def bundle_name(files, rows):
    """`bundle-<basename of the first shared file>-<4 hex of the member set>`: deterministic for the same rows,
    so a refusal is remembered by name and the same set is never added twice under two names."""
    stem = re.sub(r"[^a-z0-9]+", "-", os.path.basename(sorted(files)[0]).lower()).strip("-") or "rows"
    h = hashlib.sha1("\n".join(sorted(rows)).encode()).hexdigest()[:4]
    return f"bundle-{stem}-{h}"


def shared_by(own):
    """The files two or more of these rows name — what a second worker in the same files would collide on."""
    n = collections.Counter(f for v in own.values() for f in v)
    return sorted(f for f, c in n.items() if c >= 2)


def caps():
    return (int(os.environ.get("CC_BUNDLE_ROWS") or ROWS_MAX), int(os.environ.get("CC_BUNDLE_FILES") or FILES_MAX))


def fitted(own):
    """{row: files} -> [(shared files, rows, the rows waiting behind it)], every one within the caps. `grouped`
    joins transitively, and the first live tick after #471 joined 33 rows over 19 files through the test suite and
    two shared tools: a worker cannot finish that and a reviewer cannot read it. A GROUP OVER A CAP IS SPLIT ON
    THE FILE ITS ROWS MOST SHARE: the rows naming that file fill one bundle up to the caps, narrowest first —
    the fewest files that rows outside that set also name, then the fewest files, so a broad row (13 files on the
    live board) is the one left over rather than the one that glues. A row left over that names a file the bundle
    names WAITS for it to land — two workers in one file is what bundling is against — and the rest are grouped
    again the same way. A pair too wide for the caps on its own is no bundle: the seat's, as a lone row is."""
    rows_max, files_max = caps()
    G = brief_mod().grouped
    out, stack = [], [team for _, team in G(own)]
    while stack:
        team = stack.pop()
        sub = {k: own[k] for k in team}
        if len(team) <= rows_max and len(set().union(*sub.values())) <= files_max:
            out.append((shared_by(sub), sorted(team), []))
            continue
        count = collections.Counter(f for v in sub.values() for f in v)
        pivot = min(count, key=lambda f: (-count[f], f))
        outside = set().union(*(v for v in sub.values() if pivot not in v))
        picked, named = [], set()
        for k in sorted((k for k in team if pivot in sub[k]), key=lambda k: (len(sub[k] & outside), len(sub[k]), k)):
            if len(picked) < rows_max and len(named | sub[k]) <= files_max:
                picked.append(k); named |= sub[k]
        if not picked:      # even the narrowest row naming the pivot is over the files cap: those rows are the seat's
            stack.extend(t for _, t in G({k: v for k, v in sub.items() if pivot not in v}))
            continue
        rest = {k: v for k, v in sub.items() if k not in picked and not (v & named)}
        if len(picked) >= 2:
            out.append((shared_by({k: sub[k] for k in picked}), sorted(picked),
                        sorted(k for k in team if k not in picked and k not in rest)))
        stack.extend(t for _, t in G(rest))
    return sorted(out, key=lambda g: (-len(g[1]), g[1]))


def bundles(repo, net=True):
    """[{name, rows, files (shared), named (every file the members name), waits (rows behind it), model, titles}]
    — biggest first, or None when the board could not be read. Groups come from cc-brief's `ready`; a member
    whose brief carries milestones or whose row carries an `agent` mark is a project row and is dropped, one naming
    a file a live bundle's members name is dropped until that bundle is done, a group over the caps is split
    (fitted), and a group that drops below two rows is no bundle."""
    B = brief_mod()
    r = B.ready(repo, net=net)
    if r is None:
        return None
    free, groups, _weighed, unplaced, _blind = r
    if unplaced or not groups:
        return []
    d = B.board_of(repo) or {}
    root = d.get("path") or ""
    index = B.tracked(root) if root else {}
    tracks = d.get("tracks") or {}
    # THE FILES A LIVE BUNDLE'S MEMBERS NAME ARE TAKEN, and a row naming one is no member of another bundle. A wait
    # `fitted` computes holds only inside the tick that computed it: once the first bundle is dispatched its
    # members leave `ready` (marked `bundle`), and a bundle row with no commit yet holds no files (cc-brief's
    # held_files reads the branch), so the rows that waited would group again on the same file at the next tick
    # and start a second worker in it — the collision `show` had just promised would wait (review of #478). Read
    # off the members' own briefs, which is what the bundle's worker is editing, until the bundle row is no
    # longer live — landed, its members closed with it; abandoned, everything back in the pool.
    taken = set()
    for k, v in tracks.items():
        if isinstance(v, dict) and B.bundled(v, tracks):
            taken |= B.named(B.brief_text(repo, k), root, index)
    out = []
    for files, rows in groups:
        text = {k: B.brief_text(repo, k) for k in rows}
        # …and a bundle row is never a member of another: one that stopped is `blocked`, which is a row waiting
        # to be picked up as far as `ready` is concerned, and it would join its own members under a new name.
        # …and only a row that is `queued` with no PR: `ready` offers a `blocked` row too (DUE), and one whose
        # landing died carries a PR and commits — its work is somewhere, and the brief says a row in flight is
        # never re-bundled (review of #471).
        # …and never a row carrying an `agent` mark, WARM OR COLD. `ready` counts a mark for MARK_H and then offers
        # the row, which is right for a seat that can ask the session; a bundle asks nobody, and a row a session
        # held in its own subagent — an orch's project row above all — is that session's until it hands the row
        # back (`agent ""`), however long ago the mark was made (the brief's own line: "an orch-held project row
        # stays out even when its agent mark has gone cold").
        own = {k: B.named(text[k], root, index) for k in rows}
        members = [k for k in rows if not k.startswith("bundle-") and not MILESTONE.search(text[k])
                   and ((tracks.get(k) or {}).get("status") or "queued") == "queued"
                   and not (tracks.get(k) or {}).get("pr")
                   and not str((tracks.get(k) or {}).get("agent") or "").strip()
                   and not (own[k] & taken)]
        if len(members) < 2:
            continue
        # …and the survivors are grouped AGAIN, on the files they name themselves: `ready` joined them
        # transitively, and a row dropped just above may have been the only link — a project brief naming a dozen
        # files glued a dozen unrelated one-file rows into one bundle. A group under two rows falls out here as
        # it does in `grouped` (review of #471).
        own = {k: own[k] for k in members}
        for shared, team, waits in fitted(own):
            named = set().union(*(own[k] for k in team))
            out.append({"name": bundle_name(shared, team), "rows": team, "files": sorted(shared),
                        "named": sorted(named), "waits": waits, "model": model_for(named or set(shared), root),
                        "titles": {k: (tracks.get(k) or {}).get("title") or k for k in team}})
    return sorted(out, key=lambda b: (-len(b["rows"]), b["rows"]))


def queue_depth():
    """Landing jobs on disk, every repo — cc-land's own queue shape: one `<repo>-<pr>.json` per PR."""
    n = 0
    for p in glob.glob(os.path.join(home(), ".cc", "state", "land", "*.json")):
        try:
            with open(p) as fh:
                if (json.load(fh) or {}).get("repo"):
                    n += 1
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            continue
    return n


def holds(repo, d):
    """The first reason nothing may start now, or "" — the order the docstring gives."""
    # A PARKED PROJECT IS LEFT UNTOUCHED — asked before anything else, because everything past this point spends:
    # the judge's read at `cc-board add`, the members' marks, the worker (review of #471; DESIGN's cc-pause rule).
    pz = sh(f"{BIN}/cc-pause", "is", repo, timeout=30)
    if pz is not None and pz.returncode == 0:
        return "the project is paused (cc-pause)"
    n = queue_depth()
    if n >= QUEUE_HOLD:
        return f"the landing queue holds {n} jobs (hold at {QUEUE_HOLD})"
    t = sh(f"{BIN}/cc-tier", "allows", "goals", timeout=30)
    if t is None or t.returncode != 0:
        return "the spend tier holds work the box takes on itself (cc-tier allows goals)"
    lim = sh(f"{BIN}/cc-limit", "status", timeout=30)
    if lim is not None and lim.returncode == 0 and "(this run only)" not in (lim.stdout or ""):
        return "the box is on a usage limit (cc-limit)"
    width = int(os.environ.get("CC_BUNDLE_WIDTH") or 2)
    live = sorted(k for k, v in (d.get("tracks") or {}).items()
                  if k.startswith("bundle-") and (v.get("status") or "") in ("queued", "running", "waiting"))
    if len(live) >= width:
        return f"{len(live)} bundles already live ({', '.join(live[:3])}), width {width}"
    return ""


def compose(repo, b):
    """The one brief: the goal for the whole, then each member's brief verbatim under its own heading, and the
    Closes line. Judged like any brief when the row is added — the raised- exemption is the member rows', not
    this row's — so the frame says what each section IS: an account for the worker to scope."""
    rows, files = b["rows"], b["files"]
    shown = ", ".join(files[:3]) + (f" and {len(files) - 3} more" if len(files) > 3 else "")
    closes = ", ".join(rows[:-1]) + f" and {rows[-1]}" if len(rows) > 1 else rows[0]
    B = brief_mod()
    head = (f"GOAL: one PR that settles these {len(rows)} queued rows, whose briefs name {shown} between them: {closes}. "
            f"One worktree, one worker, one landing instead of {len(rows)}.\n\n"
            "WHY: every row costs its own landing — gates, a paid review read, a merge — and two workers in one "
            "file has cost this box a rebase and, twice, the same fix written twice. cc-bundle grouped these rows "
            "by the files their briefs name (what `cc-brief ready` prints as one builder's work).\n\n"
            "BOUNDARIES: the files these rows name and what settling them needs, nothing wider. A raised- section "
            "below is an account of what broke, for this worker to scope — the fix is the worker's to design. A "
            "row that turns out to need a design of its own is left out and named in the journal, not half-done.\n\n"
            f"DONE WHEN: every row below is settled in this one PR, or the journal names the one left out and why. "
            f"Gates run in the foreground and reported verbatim.\n\nCloses {closes}.\n")
    parts = [head]
    for k in rows:
        parts.append(f"\n## {k} — {b['titles'].get(k, k)}\n\n{B.brief_text(repo, k).strip()}\n")
    return "".join(parts)


def go(repo, dry=False, net=True, out=sys.stdout):
    """Start the first bundle nothing holds. Returns the name started, "" for nothing; prints what it did and,
    on --dry-run, what it would do. Every refusal and hold is one line in the log, so a seat reading `show`
    later sees why the backlog did not move."""
    B = brief_mod()
    d = B.board_of(repo)
    if d is None:
        return ""
    bs = bundles(repo, net=net)
    if not bs:
        return ""
    why = holds(repo, d)
    if why:
        if dry:
            print(f"{repo}: would not start {bs[0]['name']} — {why}", file=out)
        elif why != last_hold(repo):
            log(repo, "held", bs[0]["name"], rows=bs[0]["rows"], why=why)
        return ""
    refused = refused_recently(repo)
    tracks = d.get("tracks") or {}
    for b in bs:
        name = b["name"]
        if name in refused or name in tracks:
            continue          # refused inside the window, or a row of that name already exists: the seat's now
        model = MODELS[b["model"]]
        if dry:
            print(f"{repo}: would start {name} on {b['model']} — {', '.join(b['rows'])}", file=out)
            return name
        title = f"bundle: {len(b['rows'])} queued rows on {', '.join(b['files'][:2])} — {', '.join(b['rows'])}"
        r = sh(f"{BIN}/cc-board", "add", repo, name, title[:200], compose(repo, b), timeout=240)
        if r is None or r.returncode != 0:
            log(repo, "refused", name, rows=b["rows"], why=f"cc-board add: {said(r)}"[:300])
            print(f"{repo}: {name} refused at the door — {said(r)[:200]}", file=out)
            continue
        for k in b["rows"]:   # the members are marked BEFORE the launch: a crash between leaves them out of the
            sh(f"{BIN}/cc-board", "set", repo, k, "bundle", name, timeout=60)   # pool while the row is live
        r = sh(f"{BIN}/cc", repo, name, "--go", "", "--loop", LOOP, "--model", model, timeout=300)
        if r is None or r.returncode != 0:
            log(repo, "refused", name, rows=b["rows"], model=model, why=f"cc --go: {said(r)}"[:300])
            print(f"{repo}: {name} added but not started — {said(r)[:200]}", file=out)
            return ""
        log(repo, "dispatched", name, rows=b["rows"], files=b["files"], model=model)
        print(f"{repo}: started {name} on {b['model']} — {', '.join(b['rows'])}", file=out)
        return name
    return ""


def show(repo, as_json=False, net=True):
    bs = bundles(repo, net=net)
    if bs is None:
        return 0
    if as_json:
        print(json.dumps(bs, indent=1))
        return 0
    if not bs:
        return 0
    d = brief_mod().board_of(repo) or {}
    why = holds(repo, d)
    refused = refused_recently(repo)
    tracks = d.get("tracks") or {}
    print(f"{repo}: {len(bs)} bundle{'' if len(bs) == 1 else 's'} the box would run"
          + (f" — held: {why}" if why else ""))
    for b in bs:
        shown = ", ".join(b["files"][:3]) + (f" and {len(b['files']) - 3} more" if len(b["files"]) > 3 else "")
        state = (f" (refused: {refused[b['name']][:80]})" if b["name"] in refused
                 else f" (row exists [{(tracks.get(b['name']) or {}).get('status', '?')}])" if b["name"] in tracks
                 else "")
        print(f"  {b['name']} [{b['model']}] {shown}: {', '.join(b['rows'])}{state}")
        if b["waits"]:
            print(f"    {len(b['waits'])} wait behind it (they name a file it names): {', '.join(b['waits'])}")
    return 0


def tick():
    """Every repo with a board, one `go` each — from cc-reconcile's turn, every 20 min. Silent when it started
    nothing; a board that cannot be read is skipped, like everywhere else."""
    r = sh(f"{BIN}/cc-board", "boards", timeout=60)
    if r is None or r.returncode != 0:
        return 0
    for repo in (r.stdout or "").split():
        try:
            go(repo)
        except Exception as e:      # one repo's fault must not cost the others their turn
            print(f"cc-bundle: {repo}: {e}", file=sys.stderr)
    return 0


USAGE = "usage: cc-bundle show <repo> [--json] [--no-net] | go <repo> [--dry-run] [--no-net] | --tick | selfcheck"


def main(a):
    if not a:
        sys.exit(USAGE)
    if a[0] == "--tick":
        return tick()
    if a[0] == "selfcheck":
        return selfcheck()
    if len(a) < 2 or a[0] not in ("show", "go"):
        sys.exit(USAGE)
    flags = set(a[2:])
    net = "--no-net" not in flags
    if a[0] == "show":
        return show(a[1], as_json="--json" in flags, net=net)
    go(a[1], dry="--dry-run" in flags, net=net)
    return 0


# ── selfcheck ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
def selfcheck():
    import contextlib, io, shutil, tempfile
    global BIN
    p = f = 0

    def ok(name, cond):
        nonlocal p, f
        print(("ok   " if cond else "FAIL ") + name)
        p, f = p + (1 if cond else 0), f + (0 if cond else 1)

    tmp = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="cc-bundle-sc.")
    fake_home = os.path.join(tmp, "home")
    boards, state = os.path.join(fake_home, ".cc", "boards"), os.path.join(fake_home, ".cc", "state")
    os.makedirs(boards); os.makedirs(os.path.join(state, "land"))
    # cc-brief and cc-board both read their homes at import: point them here BEFORE the first import.
    os.environ.update(HOME=fake_home, CC_BOARDS=boards, CC_STATE=state, CC_BRIEF_FAKE='{"verdict":"approve"}')
    os.environ.pop("CC_BUNDLE_WIDTH", None)
    B = brief_mod()
    repo = "beta"
    src = os.path.join(tmp, "src")

    def git(*args):
        return subprocess.run(["git", "-C", src, *args], capture_output=True, text=True,
                              env={**os.environ, "GIT_AUTHOR_NAME": "t", "GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL": "t@t",
                                   "GIT_COMMITTER_NAME": "t", "GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL": "t@t"})

    subprocess.run(["git", "init", "-q", "-b", "main", src], capture_output=True)
    os.makedirs(os.path.join(src, "bin")); os.makedirs(os.path.join(src, "tests"))
    for fn in ("bin/cc-slackx", "bin/cc-guardx", "bin/other-tool", "notes.txt"):
        open(os.path.join(src, fn), "w").write("base\n")
    open(os.path.join(src, "tests", "control-layer"), "w").write("# the gate\nbin/cc-guardx\n")
    git("add", "-A"); git("commit", "-qm", "base")
    git("checkout", "-q", "-b", "track/live", "main")
    open(os.path.join(src, "notes.txt"), "a").write("live\n")
    git("add", "-A"); git("commit", "-qm", "live"); git("checkout", "-q", "main")

    def board(tracks):
        with open(os.path.join(boards, repo + ".json"), "w") as fh:
            json.dump({"repo": repo, "path": src, "default_branch": "main", "tracks": tracks, "log": []}, fh)

    def brief_of(track, text):
        d = os.path.join(state, repo, track)
        os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)
        open(os.path.join(d, "task.md"), "w").write(text)

    # ── the siblings, stubbed: `cc` records its argv; cc-tier and cc-limit answer what the case sets.
    fbin = os.path.join(tmp, "bin")
    os.makedirs(fbin)
    calls = os.path.join(tmp, "calls")
    open(os.path.join(fbin, "cc"), "w").write(
        "#!/bin/sh\nprintf '%s\\n' \"$*\" >> \"$CALLS\"\nexit \"${CC_FAKE_CC_RC:-0}\"\n")
    open(os.path.join(fbin, "cc-tier"), "w").write("#!/bin/sh\nexit \"${CC_FAKE_TIER_RC:-0}\"\n")
    open(os.path.join(fbin, "cc-pause"), "w").write("#!/bin/sh\nexit \"${CC_FAKE_PAUSE_RC:-1}\"\n")
    open(os.path.join(fbin, "cc-limit"), "w").write(
        "#!/bin/sh\n[ -n \"$CC_FAKE_LIMIT\" ] && { echo \"$CC_FAKE_LIMIT\"; exit 0; }\nexit 1\n")
    for t in ("cc-board", "cc-brief"):      # the real ones, beside this copy
        os.symlink(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__)), t), os.path.join(fbin, t))
    for fn in os.listdir(fbin):
        os.chmod(os.path.join(fbin, fn), 0o755)
    os.environ["CALLS"] = calls
    BIN = fbin

    def calls_made():
        try:
            return open(calls).read().splitlines()
        except OSError:
            return []

    # ── what a bundle is
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued", "title": "a is wrong"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued", "title": "b too"},
           "row-c": {"status": "queued", "title": "c stands alone"}, "row-d": {"status": "queued"},
           "row-e": {"status": "queued"}})
    brief_of("row-a", "GOAL: bin/cc-slackx says the wrong thing.\n")
    brief_of("row-b", "GOAL: bin/cc-slackx says another wrong thing.\n")
    brief_of("row-c", "GOAL: notes.txt on its own.\n")
    brief_of("row-d", "GOAL: bin/cc-guardx refuses a thing, and bin/other-tool with it.\n")
    brief_of("row-e", "GOAL: bin/other-tool prints the wrong line.\n")
    bs = bundles(repo)
    ok("two queued rows naming one file are a bundle, and a row sharing nothing is not in any",
       bs is not None and [b["rows"] for b in bs] == [["row-a", "row-b"], ["row-d", "row-e"]])
    one = next(b for b in bs if b["rows"] == ["row-a", "row-b"])
    ok("a bundle on one file outside the control layer runs on Sonnet", one["model"] == "sonnet")
    two = next(b for b in bs if b["rows"] == ["row-d", "row-e"])
    ok("…and one that names a control-layer file, or more than one file, runs on Opus", two["model"] == "opus")
    ok("the name carries the shared file and a hash of the member set", re.fullmatch(r"bundle-cc-slackx-[0-9a-f]{4}", one["name"]) is not None
       and bundle_name(["bin/cc-slackx"], ["row-a", "row-b"]) == one["name"] and bundle_name(["bin/cc-slackx"], ["row-a", "x"]) != one["name"])
    ok("the shared files and everything the members name are both reported",
       one["files"] == ["bin/cc-slackx"] and two["named"] == ["bin/cc-guardx", "bin/other-tool"])

    text = compose(repo, one)
    ok("the composed brief closes every member, so the bundle's PR closes them all when it lands",
       "Closes row-a and row-b." in text)
    ok("…and carries each member's brief verbatim under its own heading",
       "## row-a — a is wrong" in text and "bin/cc-slackx says another wrong thing" in text)
    ok("…and says what a raised- section is, for the judge", "account of what broke" in text)

    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued"}, "proj": {"status": "queued"}})
    brief_of("proj", "GOAL: a knowledge library.\nM1: bin/cc-slackx learns to write to it.\nM2: the rest.\n")
    ok("a project row — a brief with milestones — stays whole: dropped from the group it would join",
       [b["rows"] for b in bundles(repo)] == [["row-a", "row-b"]])
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued"}, "proj": {"status": "queued"}})
    ok("…and a group left with one row is no bundle", bundles(repo) == [])
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued"}, "row-d": {"status": "queued"}, "proj": {"status": "queued"}})
    brief_of("proj", "GOAL: a library.\nM1: bin/cc-slackx writes to it.\nM2: bin/cc-guardx reads it.\n")
    ok("…and a project row that was the only link between two rows sharing nothing leaves no bundle behind",
       bundles(repo) == [])
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued"}, "proj": {"status": "queued"}})
    brief_of("proj", "GOAL: a loop.\nSHAPE PROPOSED (the orch decides): M1 the scorer on bin/cc-slackx, M2 the loop.\n")
    ok("a brief numbering its milestones mid-line (M1 … M2, no line of their own) is a project row too",
       [b["rows"] for b in bundles(repo)] == [["row-a", "row-b"]])
    brief_of("proj", "GOAL: bin/cc-slackx, plainly.\n")
    ok("…and the same row with a plain brief is a member", [b["rows"] for b in bundles(repo)] == [["proj", "row-a", "row-b"]])
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued"},
           "proj": {"status": "queued", "agent": "@1:2", "agent_at": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"}})
    ok("a row whose agent mark went cold is offered by `ready`, and is no member here: nobody handed it back",
       [b["rows"] for b in bundles(repo)] == [["row-a", "row-b"]])
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued"},
           "proj": {"status": "queued", "agent": "@1:2", "agent_at": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())}})
    ok("…nor is one whose mark is warm", [b["rows"] for b in bundles(repo)] == [["row-a", "row-b"]])
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued"}, "proj": {"status": "queued", "agent": "", "agent_at": ""}})
    ok("…and a row handed back (`agent \"\"`) is a member again", [b["rows"] for b in bundles(repo)] == [["proj", "row-a", "row-b"]])

    # ── the caps: a group over one is split on the file its rows most share, and what it leaves waits
    rows = {f"r{i}": {"status": "queued"} for i in range(1, 8)}
    rows.update({"glue": {"status": "queued"}, "s1": {"status": "queued"}, "s2": {"status": "queued"}})
    board(rows)
    for i in range(1, 8):
        brief_of(f"r{i}", f"GOAL: bin/other-tool prints line {i} wrong.\n")
    brief_of("glue", "GOAL: bin/other-tool and bin/cc-slackx disagree.\n")
    brief_of("s1", "GOAL: bin/cc-slackx, one thing.\n"); brief_of("s2", "GOAL: bin/cc-slackx, another.\n")
    bs = bundles(repo)
    ok("ten rows one broad row glues are not one bundle: the file most of them share takes ROWS_MAX of them, the "
       "rest are grouped again on their own",
       [b["rows"] for b in bs] == [["r1", "r2", "r3", "r4", "r5", "r6"], ["s1", "s2"]])
    ok("…the rows left over that name a file it names wait behind it, the broad one among them",
       bs[0]["waits"] == ["glue", "r7"] and bs[1]["waits"] == [])
    ok("…and bundles offered together name no file in common", not (set(bs[0]["named"]) & set(bs[1]["named"])))
    buf = io.StringIO()
    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(buf):
        show(repo)
    ok("…and `show` says which rows wait", "2 wait behind it (they name a file it names): glue, r7" in buf.getvalue())
    board({f"r{i}": {"status": "queued"} for i in range(1, 7)})
    bs = bundles(repo)
    ok("a group at the cap is offered whole", [b["rows"] for b in bs] == [["r1", "r2", "r3", "r4", "r5", "r6"]] and bs[0]["waits"] == [])
    # …and the wait holds ACROSS ticks, not only inside the one that computed it (review of #478): the dispatched
    # bundle's members leave `ready`, and its row holds no files until the worker commits, so the rows that waited
    # would have grouped again on the same file at the next tick and started a second worker in it.
    board(rows)
    open(calls, "w").close()
    went = go(repo, out=io.StringIO())
    tr = B.board_of(repo).get("tracks") or {}
    first = bundle_name(["bin/other-tool"], [f"r{i}" for i in range(1, 7)])
    ok("go starts the first bundle of a split and marks its members",
       went == first and all(tr[f"r{i}"].get("bundle") == first for i in range(1, 7)))

    def edit(fn):
        pth = os.path.join(boards, repo + ".json")
        with open(pth) as fh:
            dd = json.load(fh)
        fn(dd["tracks"])
        with open(pth, "w") as fh:
            json.dump(dd, fh)
    ok("…and while its row is live with no commit, the rows that waited are still no bundle, the rest still are",
       [b["rows"] for b in bundles(repo)] == [["s1", "s2"]])
    edit(lambda t: t[first].update(status="running"))
    ok("…the same once it is running", [b["rows"] for b in bundles(repo)] == [["s1", "s2"]])

    def landed(t):
        t[first].update(status="done")
        for i in range(1, 7):
            t[f"r{i}"].update(status="done")
    edit(landed)
    ok("…and once it has landed, they are grouped again", [b["rows"] for b in bundles(repo)] == [["glue", "r7", "s1", "s2"]])
    open(calls, "w").close()
    os.environ["CC_BUNDLE_FILES"] = "2"
    board({"f1": {"status": "queued"}, "f2": {"status": "queued"}, "f3": {"status": "queued"}})
    brief_of("f1", "GOAL: bin/other-tool and notes.txt.\n")
    brief_of("f2", "GOAL: bin/other-tool and bin/cc-guardx.\n")
    brief_of("f3", "GOAL: bin/other-tool alone.\n")
    ok("the files cap (here CC_BUNDLE_FILES=2) splits the same way: the narrowest rows fill it, the one that would "
       "widen it waits", [(b["rows"], b["named"], b["waits"]) for b in bundles(repo)]
       == [(["f1", "f3"], ["bin/other-tool", "notes.txt"], ["f2"])])
    board({"p": {"status": "queued"}, "q": {"status": "queued"}, "s1": {"status": "queued"}, "s2": {"status": "queued"}})
    brief_of("p", "GOAL: bin/other-tool, notes.txt and bin/cc-guardx.\n")
    brief_of("q", "GOAL: bin/other-tool, notes.txt and tests/control-layer.\n")
    ok("…and a pair too wide for it on its own is no bundle — the seat's — and costs the rows beside it nothing",
       [b["rows"] for b in bundles(repo)] == [["s1", "s2"]])
    os.environ.pop("CC_BUNDLE_FILES")

    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued"},
           "live": {"status": "review", "branch": "track/live", "pr": "1"}})
    brief_of("row-a", "GOAL: notes.txt is held by the live row.\n")
    brief_of("row-b", "GOAL: notes.txt as well.\n")
    ok("rows sharing a file a live track holds are not offered — `ready` calls neither free", bundles(repo) == [])
    brief_of("row-a", "GOAL: bin/cc-slackx says the wrong thing.\n")
    brief_of("row-b", "GOAL: bin/cc-slackx says another wrong thing.\n")
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued"}, "died": {"status": "blocked", "pr": "7", "branch": "track/live"}})
    brief_of("died", "GOAL: bin/cc-slackx, whose landing died with the PR open.\n")
    ok("a blocked row with a PR — a landing that died — is in flight, not a member: no bundle with the queued row",
       bundles(repo) == [])
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued", "pr": "8"}})
    ok("…nor is a queued row that already carries a PR", bundles(repo) == [])
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued"}, "row-b": {"status": "blocked"}})
    ok("…nor a blocked row without one: only `queued` rows are members", bundles(repo) == [])

    # ── the holds, each on its own fixture, and the dispatch
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued", "title": "a is wrong"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued", "title": "b too"}})
    for i in range(QUEUE_HOLD):
        open(os.path.join(state, "land", f"x-{i}.json"), "w").write(json.dumps({"repo": "x", "pr": str(i)}))
    os.environ["CC_FAKE_PAUSE_RC"] = "0"
    ok("a parked project holds it before anything else, and says so",
       holds(repo, B.board_of(repo)) == "the project is paused (cc-pause)")
    went = go(repo, out=io.StringIO())
    tr = B.board_of(repo).get("tracks") or {}
    ok("…and `go` on a parked project adds no row, marks no member and starts nothing — the board is untouched",
       went == "" and sorted(tr) == ["row-a", "row-b"] and not any(tr[k].get("bundle") for k in tr)
       and calls_made() == [])
    os.environ.pop("CC_FAKE_PAUSE_RC")
    try:
        os.remove(log_path(repo))   # the hold it logged; the queue cases below count their own lines
    except OSError:
        pass
    ok("the landing queue at the hold stops a dispatch, and says so", "landing queue holds 4" in holds(repo, B.board_of(repo)))
    os.remove(os.path.join(state, "land", "x-0.json"))
    ok("…and one job under it does not", holds(repo, B.board_of(repo)) == "")
    os.environ["CC_FAKE_TIER_RC"] = "1"
    ok("the spend tier holds it", "spend tier" in holds(repo, B.board_of(repo)))
    os.environ.pop("CC_FAKE_TIER_RC")
    os.environ["CC_FAKE_LIMIT"] = "usage limit until 18:00"
    ok("a box-wide usage limit holds it", "usage limit" in holds(repo, B.board_of(repo)))
    os.environ["CC_FAKE_LIMIT"] = "usage limit until 18:00 (this run only)"
    ok("…but one run's own limit is not the box's", holds(repo, B.board_of(repo)) == "")
    os.environ.pop("CC_FAKE_LIMIT")
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued"}, "bundle-p-0000": {"status": "running"},
           "bundle-q-0000": {"status": "queued"}})
    ok("two bundles already live is the width, and a third waits", "2 bundles already live" in holds(repo, B.board_of(repo)))
    os.environ["CC_BUNDLE_WIDTH"] = "3"
    ok("…and CC_BUNDLE_WIDTH widens it", holds(repo, B.board_of(repo)) == "")
    os.environ.pop("CC_BUNDLE_WIDTH")

    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued", "title": "a is wrong"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued", "title": "b too"}})
    for i in range(QUEUE_HOLD):
        open(os.path.join(state, "land", f"x-{i}.json"), "w").write(json.dumps({"repo": "x", "pr": str(i)}))
    go(repo, dry=True, out=io.StringIO())
    ok("a dry run under a hold writes nothing", not os.path.exists(log_path(repo)))
    go(repo, out=io.StringIO()); go(repo, out=io.StringIO())
    ok("a hold is logged once, not once per tick while it stands",
       [json.loads(l)["event"] for l in open(log_path(repo))] == ["held"])
    for i in range(QUEUE_HOLD):
        os.remove(os.path.join(state, "land", f"x-{i}.json"))
    os.remove(log_path(repo))
    buf = io.StringIO()
    went = go(repo, dry=True, out=buf)
    ok("--dry-run names the bundle and the model and starts nothing",
       went == one["name"] and "would start bundle-cc-slackx" in buf.getvalue() and "sonnet" in buf.getvalue()
       and calls_made() == [] and one["name"] not in (B.board_of(repo).get("tracks") or {}))
    buf = io.StringIO()
    went = go(repo, out=buf)
    tr = B.board_of(repo).get("tracks") or {}
    ok("go adds the bundle row through cc-board add, with the composed brief as its task",
       went == one["name"] and one["name"] in tr and "Closes row-a and row-b." in B.brief_text(repo, one["name"]))
    ok("…marks every member `bundle: <row>` and leaves it queued",
       all(tr[k].get("bundle") == one["name"] and tr[k].get("status") == "queued" for k in ("row-a", "row-b")))
    ok("…starts the worker with `cc <repo> <row> --go \"\"` on the band's model, --loop 3",
       calls_made() == [f"{repo} {one['name']} --go  --loop 3 --model claude-sonnet-5"])
    ok("…logs the dispatch", any(json.loads(l)["event"] == "dispatched" for l in open(log_path(repo))))
    ok("…and the members are out of the pool while the bundle row is live: nothing to run now",
       bundles(repo) == [] and set(B.candidates(B.board_of(repo))) == {one["name"]})
    buf = io.StringIO()
    ok("a second go starts nothing and prints nothing", go(repo, out=buf) == "" and buf.getvalue() == "")

    # …a bundle row that already exists is not added twice, whatever its status
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued"}, one["name"]: {"status": "blocked"}})
    open(calls, "w").close()
    ok("a bundle whose row already exists (here blocked) is left to the seat, not re-added or re-started",
       go(repo, out=io.StringIO()) == "" and calls_made() == [])

    # …and a refusal at the door is recorded and not retried inside the window
    os.remove(log_path(repo))
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued", "title": "row-a"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued", "title": "row-b"}})
    os.environ["CC_BRIEF_FAKE"] = '{"verdict":"reject","why":"it prescribes","cut":["says the wrong thing"]}'
    buf = io.StringIO()
    went = go(repo, out=buf)
    tr = B.board_of(repo).get("tracks") or {}
    ok("the judge's refusal at cc-board add stops the bundle: no row, no marks, no worker, said and logged",
       went == "" and "refused at the door" in buf.getvalue() and one["name"] not in tr
       and not tr["row-a"].get("bundle") and calls_made() == [] and one["name"] in refused_recently(repo))
    os.environ["CC_BRIEF_FAKE"] = '{"verdict":"approve"}'
    ok("…and the same set is not offered again inside the window",
       go(repo, dry=True, out=io.StringIO()) == "")
    os.remove(log_path(repo))

    # …and `cc` refusing the launch (a paused project, the tier at the row) leaves the row for the seat
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued", "title": "row-a"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued", "title": "row-b"}})
    os.environ["CC_FAKE_CC_RC"] = "1"
    buf = io.StringIO()
    went = go(repo, out=buf)
    ok("`cc --go` refusing leaves the added row and its marks for the seat, and logs the refusal",
       went == "" and "added but not started" in buf.getvalue()
       and any(json.loads(l)["event"] == "refused" for l in open(log_path(repo))))
    os.environ.pop("CC_FAKE_CC_RC")

    # ── show
    os.remove(log_path(repo))
    board({"row-a": {"status": "queued", "title": "row-a"}, "row-b": {"status": "queued", "title": "row-b"}})
    buf = io.StringIO()
    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(buf):
        show(repo)
    ok("show prints each bundle with its model, files and rows",
       "1 bundle the box would run" in buf.getvalue() and f"{one['name']} [sonnet] bin/cc-slackx: row-a, row-b" in buf.getvalue())
    buf = io.StringIO()
    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(buf):
        show(repo, as_json=True)
    ok("…and --json is the same answer as data", json.loads(buf.getvalue())[0]["rows"] == ["row-a", "row-b"])
    for i in range(QUEUE_HOLD):
        open(os.path.join(state, "land", f"x-{i}.json"), "w").write(json.dumps({"repo": "x", "pr": str(i)}))
    buf = io.StringIO()
    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(buf):
        show(repo)
    ok("…and names what holds them", "held: the landing queue holds 4" in buf.getvalue())
    board({"row-c": {"status": "queued"}})
    buf = io.StringIO()
    with contextlib.redirect_stdout(buf):
        show(repo)
    ok("nothing to run prints nothing", buf.getvalue() == "")

    shutil.rmtree(tmp, ignore_errors=True)
    print(f"\ncc-bundle selfcheck: {p} passed, {f} failed")
    return 1 if f else 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
